    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0816" n="721" xml:id="pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/563: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-26T17:00:00-05:00">February 26, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Unless you perceive objection, please communicate to the Japanese Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs as from me a message reading as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“On behalf of the American Government and people I assure you of the deep
                            regret with which we have learned of the death of distinguished
                            officials of the Japanese Government and I extend to you our sincere
                            condolences.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Report action by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
